name intercept-aim120-1
timeout 280

# THE INTERCEPT: the first shot with a guided weapon, end to end and measurable at every step.
#
# Two jets, head-on, co-altitude, level and constant-speed, so the true geometry is a straight line the
# analysis can recompute from the two telemetry files alone (the same discipline as the radar missions):
#
#   viper   flies due EAST  from 46.900/6.600 at 8,000 m -- the shooter. ACM HUD scan with the range
#           gate opened to the full 40 nm, so the auto-lock happens on the first sweeps and the whole run
#           is about the WEAPON rather than about acquiring.
#   bandit  flies due WEST  from 46.900/7.300 at 8,000 m -- the target. Radar OFF: it contributes a
#           radar cross-section and nothing else, and it does not manoeuvre, so the miss distance is a
#           property of the guidance and not of the target's evasion.
#
# They start 53 km apart and close at roughly 630 m/s (both true-airspeed ~315 m/s at this altitude).
#
# THE SHOT is a briefed pickle at t=20 s, i.e. at ~40 km / 22 nm: comfortably inside Raero and far
# outside Rmin, so the SMS accepts it and the launch record (events.log "LAUNCH_SOLUTION") carries the
# whole launch zone the fire control computed. What has to be visible in the missile's own telemetry
# afterwards is the entire flight of the round:
#   - the boost (msl_* columns beside a rising speed in the FDM columns), the sustain, then the coast
#   - msl_phase INERTIAL -> MIDCOURSE (the launcher's uplink arriving) -> TERMINAL (its own seeker)
#   - msl_seeker 0 -> 1 at the activation range -> 2 when it locks
#   - msl_losrate: proportional navigation driving the line-of-sight rate toward zero
#   - the DETONATION event with the miss distance, the closing speed and the geometry
#
# Both jets have a waypoint at the end of their leg, and a weapon's flight is an EVENT inside a mission
# rather than the mission's verdict. Since the damage model exists (core/FBDamageModel), though, the
# round that arrives here is decisive after all: the burst destroys the bandit's systems, the bandit's
# own mission monitor concludes FAIL ("combat ineffective") and the RUN ENDS AT THE HIT — exit 1, at
# ~70.4 s, instead of the SUCCESS at ~191 s this mission used to report. Everything up to that tick is
# unchanged, column for column; what the missile did is measured exactly as before.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.60000 8000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40                      # the ACM box, range gate opened to the search figure
  set store 3 aim120                       # left wing pylon
  set store 7 aim120                       # its mirror on the right wing
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 20                   # ~22 nm, head-on: inside the launch zone
  wp 46.90000 7.15000 8000 400          # 42 km east: reached at ~205 s, so the run ends SUCCESS

unit bandit
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.30000 8000 270.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  wp 46.90000 6.75000 8000 400          # its mirror leg west
